WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:01.840
There we go.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:04.960
We've got

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.760
the recording going.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.120
And three things on the public hearing tonight,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.000
and

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:16.865
we'll take them just as in the order on the agenda.

00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:19.345
But the first item up is

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:21.665
the discussion of

00:00:22.065 --> 00:00:24.785
proposed amendments to the zoning regulations,

00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:26.385
more particularly

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.220
section 15 signs in their entirety.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.180
So that's what we're going to talk about first.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.980
Abby, if you can let me share my screen.

00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:42.795
Okay, you're all set, Jed.

00:00:49.835 --> 00:00:50.715
>> Okay,

00:00:50.715 --> 00:00:52.715
and so this is

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:56.450
the latest version of the sign regs. So

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:01.890
I just wanted to give a little overview on what we were doing and walk through.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:02.930
I think

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:10.055
there's a couple of people here that are probably interested in what we're doing with election signs and political signs.

00:01:10.615 --> 00:01:13.815
And so I wanted to address that and then we'll

00:01:14.135 --> 00:01:15.735
take whatever comments

00:01:15.815 --> 00:01:16.695
anybody

00:01:17.175 --> 00:01:17.895
has

00:01:18.375 --> 00:01:19.495
there. But

00:01:20.535 --> 00:01:22.375
during the last

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:25.820
two year election,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:27.980
we

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.340
discovered that there were some

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.660
unconstitutional

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.540
aspects

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.380
of our signed regulations.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.100
And essentially,

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:40.225
though we had put a limit on

00:01:41.665 --> 00:01:43.745
people being able to

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:47.505
put their signs up to

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:50.705
about thirty days prior to election and

00:01:51.105 --> 00:01:52.305
that's certainly

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.780
not conducive to when the campaign season starts anymore.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.100
There was some confusion on the number of

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.460
number and sizes of the different signs.

00:02:07.485 --> 00:02:10.365
And then during the pandemic we saw

00:02:10.845 --> 00:02:12.285
a lot of signs

00:02:12.285 --> 00:02:13.565
going out. So

00:02:15.005 --> 00:02:19.725
one of the things I thought I would do when I started tackling

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.890
design regulations

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.210
is fix all the ills.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.370
I rapidly discovered that was not going to be possible,

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.490
so I

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:29.850
cut my

00:02:31.945 --> 00:02:40.425
goal back to making sure that we didn't have any violations of anybody's constitutional rights and so that's where we're at and we did

00:02:40.825 --> 00:02:44.105
make some changes to try and improve a few things but

00:02:44.905 --> 00:02:45.305
anyhow.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:52.980
So we noted up here in the intent while ensuring constitutional right of free speech is protected.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.540
I

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:04.635
came to find out there were really two kinds of political signs. There's

00:03:05.195 --> 00:03:08.075
political signs where people are stating

00:03:08.315 --> 00:03:10.715
their views or opinions,

00:03:11.995 --> 00:03:13.995
and then there's signs

00:03:13.995 --> 00:03:15.595
for

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:15.880
candidates.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.840
And we broke those two things into two different sections here.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.120
So,

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.200
you know, the political position sign, that would be a sign something like

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:35.855
we support the police or defund the police or any of those kind of things that you might see that that provide a political viewpoint.

00:03:36.495 --> 00:03:40.895
And then then there's the signs that we would put up prior to an election.

00:03:42.095 --> 00:03:44.175
And that's that's what we show there.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.160
You can see here that I did find some last minute

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.240
errors into my numbering system, so I fixed that up as I went through getting ready for tonight.

00:04:01.495 --> 00:04:08.935
We also did away with a roof sign. Know, nobody in Andover's got a sign up on the roof. We didn't think

00:04:09.575 --> 00:04:13.335
that was what we wanted to see here, and we eliminated that.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.070
A vehicular sign, if somebody's parking

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:25.710
a big box truck with an advertising banner on it near the road for an extended period of time where it's not normally parked, we wanted

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:26.430
to do that.

00:04:28.795 --> 00:04:32.235
I did add, you know, a word on banner signs.

00:04:33.275 --> 00:04:33.835
And

00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:37.755
it was tough to figure out

00:04:38.235 --> 00:04:41.515
when does a banner differ from a flag

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.860
and all that kind of thing. So there's probably going to be some

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:50.860
differences there. I just didn't want any political banners going up over the Andover

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.435
Rail Trail Bridge.

00:04:55.235 --> 00:04:56.675
And then I took

00:04:57.235 --> 00:05:08.515
a sentence out of one of our ordinances that I figured if we had an ordinance about no signage being at the Veterans Monument, I would put that in our sign range. I thought that was a good place for that.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.100
Here's

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:17.380
a part that probably will be, you know, a little bit of concern to some folks and

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.580
this is no change from the preceding

00:05:22.885 --> 00:05:24.965
version of our regulations.

00:05:25.365 --> 00:05:32.965
It says all signs or part thereof shall be clear of all street right of ways and no closer than 15 feet to the lot line.

00:05:35.125 --> 00:05:37.445
I know there are

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.430
signs that, you know, we have right out next to the road

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.350
in the town right away.

00:05:49.785 --> 00:05:55.145
And since we haven't changed any of the wording on that, you know, my thought was that

00:05:58.505 --> 00:06:02.825
there hasn't been any problems in the past, might not be any problems in the future. My

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:09.400
rationale and I was going to take this out, I left it in because I thought that

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:16.920
with the, you know, all the political statements everybody wants to make and put a sign out there,

00:06:18.495 --> 00:06:25.535
I didn't want political signs. I didn't think political signs should be on town property expressing

00:06:25.855 --> 00:06:27.055
people's views.

00:06:27.695 --> 00:06:31.055
And so that included, you know, with the right of way out

00:06:31.055 --> 00:06:31.455
here too.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:44.540
And if I allow one sign to be in the right of way, I have to allow for freedom of speech any sign to be in the right of way. And so that's why no change, but I didn't get rid of that restriction either.

00:06:48.015 --> 00:06:51.375
Coming down, you know, we used to specify that

00:06:52.095 --> 00:06:55.055
a temporary sign which included an election sign

00:06:56.415 --> 00:07:00.015
couldn't be up more than thirty days prior to an election and

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.230
we got rid of that part.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:07.750
Now say that, you know, no more than seven days after the event

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:08.630
the

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:14.870
event has concluded, whether it be an election, tag sale, you have it, the sign should be removed.

00:07:19.575 --> 00:07:27.015
Now we get into the size of the sign. So for an election sign, you know, can be a freestanding sign

00:07:27.015 --> 00:07:31.520
up to 32 square feet in the business area or industrial zone

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.240
and 16 square feet in the residential zone.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:39.600
Last time around, we said that everybody could have a 32 square foot sign

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:45.145
because we thought it had to be equivalent to the largest sign

00:07:45.385 --> 00:07:46.585
in our town.

00:07:48.105 --> 00:07:49.545
It turns out the

00:07:50.265 --> 00:07:54.425
ruling on that's been clarified a little bit, and so we have to allow

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.080
election signs to be as big as any other sign in that zone.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:04.360
So in the residential zones, maximum size was signed with 16 square feet,

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.840
and so we reduced it down to that too.

00:08:08.115 --> 00:08:08.755
The

00:08:09.395 --> 00:08:10.595
other thing that

00:08:10.755 --> 00:08:16.355
we continue to allow is I know people want to put up multiple signs for multiple candidates.

00:08:17.155 --> 00:08:25.840
And so we allowed if it's in the business or industrial zone of 50 square feet total. So you can have a 32 square feet sign

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:32.560
that gives you 18 square feet for other two square foot signs. You can have another nine

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:33.760
little signs if you want.

00:08:34.545 --> 00:08:39.425
In the residential zone, we lowered that to 32 square feet total.

00:08:39.825 --> 00:08:44.545
So again, 16 square feet, that gives you eight more little signs to put in your yard.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:54.400
Oh, I added no trespassing signs. As I walked around, I saw a bunch of no trespassing signs. Thought that would be

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:55.840
pretty reasonable.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.840
Political position signs.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:04.925
Each lot may have one sign, maximum 16 square feet in residential zone, 33 square feet in a business zone.

00:09:05.565 --> 00:09:09.805
No political position sign shall be allowed on publicly owned property.

00:09:09.965 --> 00:09:10.045
And

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:16.510
so that's it. That was our thought on that.

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.870
That doesn't mean you can't put up the

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:22.270
fire department steak fry,

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:27.630
you know, sign that I frequently see over at the dump and that kind of stuff when

00:09:27.955 --> 00:09:29.475
time comes around for that.

00:09:32.275 --> 00:09:32.915
So,

00:09:34.115 --> 00:09:36.515
I think that's what I wanted to point out in here.

00:09:37.155 --> 00:09:40.035
The, you know, going back to

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:43.580
the

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:48.940
rationale for what we did with the election signs and that,

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:50.220
you know,

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.500
it is recognized when you have zoning

00:09:53.745 --> 00:09:55.985
laws, zoning regulations,

00:09:56.385 --> 00:10:01.185
that a regulation may not be optimum for every lot in the zone.

00:10:03.345 --> 00:10:09.105
And that's why anybody who has a planning and zoning commission also has to have a zoning board of appeals.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:11.960
And so if

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.520
you think that your lot

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.200
isn't

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.480
is special, needs a special consideration with respect to our

00:10:21.815 --> 00:10:23.415
zoning regulations.

00:10:23.735 --> 00:10:26.375
One of the actions you could take would be to go

00:10:26.695 --> 00:10:28.535
to the zoning board of appeals.

00:10:29.255 --> 00:10:32.535
The other thing you could do is you could put your sign up in

00:10:33.095 --> 00:10:34.695
agent Halsey is

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:35.720
pretty.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.000
He

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:44.520
has a lot of discretion about you know where he sees violations and which ones he's going to pursue and that sort of thing.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:50.280
And if you're doing the best you can to comply with that just as in the past you probably

00:10:50.655 --> 00:10:51.535
won't

00:10:52.255 --> 00:10:57.135
won't hear too much about that. But I did want to have something in there that if somebody

00:10:57.535 --> 00:11:00.175
put in a sign that we thought was

00:11:01.215 --> 00:11:02.495
totally inappropriate,

00:11:02.495 --> 00:11:05.055
we did have a mechanism to at least

00:11:05.470 --> 00:11:09.630
push it back onto their own property as opposed to having on the town right away.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:18.430
The other thing that we did is in our current regulations, there's some words in there that say

00:11:18.745 --> 00:11:21.385
if you do put a sign up in the town right away,

00:11:21.945 --> 00:11:25.065
the zoning agent can go take the sign down.

00:11:26.025 --> 00:11:30.825
And we remove those words, just like we think that, you know, we have

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:33.500
the approach

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.220
that

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:39.580
if you you don't like the words in here you can appeal to the zoning board of appeals.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:47.615
Agent Halsey has a process that he goes through if he sees an infraction of the zone and so that's

00:11:48.255 --> 00:11:53.775
a little more cumbersome on his behalf too. So I would like to think that

00:11:56.895 --> 00:11:57.615
we

00:11:57.855 --> 00:12:00.175
can with these protect free speech,

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:05.760
allow you to put up lots of signs as early as you want supportive of an election and

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.560
live happily ever after.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:13.520
And with that you know I am happy to

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:17.440
entertain any comments from the public.

00:12:18.125 --> 00:12:18.925
And I guess

00:12:20.845 --> 00:12:21.885
I see,

00:12:23.325 --> 00:12:26.045
well, I'd like to try and have

00:12:26.445 --> 00:12:28.045
people raise their hand.

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:37.610
I'm going to try and avoid having Abby call on each person individually to save a little time because we've got three hearings that we want to go through and I'd like to

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:43.770
to focus on those folks who've got a comment on the sign regulations at this point.

00:12:49.255 --> 00:12:52.615
Anybody got any comments on the signs? Carol?

00:12:53.575 --> 00:12:57.415
>> I understand and the 15 feet from the road

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:03.120
but it's very hard when you live like around the lake or your driveway is just the driveway

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:08.080
and you're right at your, you know, there's trees and bushes and everything

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:14.785
on your property. That means that if like for me, if I put it up 15 feet from the road,

00:13:15.265 --> 00:13:18.945
which I try to do, I'm almost into my facility of bushes.

00:13:19.585 --> 00:13:28.320
Yep. And other people, they've got their dry, it's just their driveway and then they have all the trees and the bushes that are right along the road

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.600
and 15 feet would mean they're into the woods.

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.880
So nobody would see their sign.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:43.175
So when they try to put it where they don't want to block their view from getting into the road, other people's view in the road.

00:13:43.815 --> 00:13:44.295
What

00:13:44.695 --> 00:13:49.655
was the sense of them even getting a sign if they can't put it somewhere where it could be seen?

00:13:51.015 --> 00:13:51.975
>> So,

00:13:52.615 --> 00:13:56.210
was out doing my morning walk today and

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:04.370
I knew you would ask that question so I paid particular attention to your percythia bushes as I walked down that way.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:05.170
And

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.650
I have seen

00:14:08.695 --> 00:14:11.975
election signs out in front of your house before.

00:14:12.135 --> 00:14:12.695
Would

00:14:13.335 --> 00:14:14.375
ask that you,

00:14:15.495 --> 00:14:16.935
right now there's a

00:14:17.655 --> 00:14:18.615
River

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:37.905
Valley Tree Service sign out in front of your house that's kind of overgrown with the percythia bush that's kind of even hard to see but it's been there for a long time. Yeah, I'll get my son to get that out of there. Okay, but anyhow, so if you were to trim that lower stuff and you put it just on this side of the prosithia bush,

00:14:38.225 --> 00:14:42.705
I think agent Halsey would probably give you credit for having tried

00:14:44.145 --> 00:14:47.425
your best to meet that. I think agent Halsey's

00:14:47.425 --> 00:14:58.610
got enough irons in the fire right now that that's probably not the the biggest issue that he's got. Well, the only issue would be is that the town supposed to mow my front of my property

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:06.805
>> and it's in need of being mowed and I don't know when the town's going to go around mowing sides of the road efficiently

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:12.565
and high enough to make it be seen. It's not my I can't mow my front of my rocks.

00:15:13.285 --> 00:15:18.165
I can mow maybe near my forsythias but I can't mow the rocks and the rocks have the weeds.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:21.530
Nope and you put you normally put your signs

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:28.010
>> behind the rocks in front of the bushes. Right but they got to get mowed so they haven't seen. Okay yep well

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:30.250
>> I'm

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:36.455
not here to solve the weed know that's Eric's issue. But I understand and

00:15:36.855 --> 00:15:38.055
I worked,

00:15:38.935 --> 00:15:39.895
tried to

00:15:40.375 --> 00:15:44.055
work very hard on how to accommodate those different

00:15:44.775 --> 00:15:46.055
situations like yours.

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.420
>> Because I know some people on the lake,

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:56.060
another RTC member, 15 feet is basically at her front door.

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:57.260
>> Well,

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:16.025
and so I was hoping she was here so I didn't talk about her with her not being in attendance. Don't see her here, but I noticed that's where she has two or three signs right now. Because she saw your probably the email I sent out so she made sure she was putting them. Yep. But then it's on you you you don't see really see them unless you're

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.480
>> you look at our house.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:27.440
This is where I I you know when you go around the lake and you see people their driveways go down their yards go down and 15 feet down

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:33.055
is is down and it's like nobody's going to see a sign there and that's where it gets a little hard.

00:16:33.295 --> 00:16:36.095
Okay. I understand the site and everything but

00:16:37.215 --> 00:16:39.535
all we can do is try to work with it.

00:16:40.575 --> 00:16:43.295
>> In the town will, I'm sure. Yeah.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.250
Anybody

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.210
else have

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.210
a comment on that?

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:52.010
>> I also do. I wanted to

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:53.450
mention

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.490
also the issue around the lake.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:57.930
Not only are they short,

00:17:00.305 --> 00:17:01.185
I'm

00:17:01.185 --> 00:17:02.145
sorry, one

00:17:04.785 --> 00:17:09.505
of the problems at the beginning of the lake where there are people who have really long driveways,

00:17:09.985 --> 00:17:15.770
you don't see the homes and the trees, the heavy woods goes all the way to the road.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:32.045
And it's not just around the lake, but a lot of people in Andover since we're so country have the same issue. You're not seeing their house and their heavy woods goes all the way to the road. So I just don't think it's fair that not everybody will be able to participate in

00:17:32.365 --> 00:17:34.205
putting up signs of their choosing.

00:17:35.725 --> 00:17:38.285
>> I didn't say that you couldn't participate.

00:17:38.605 --> 00:17:40.765
Said that you would be able, if you wanted,

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:46.300
you could go the more cumbersome route, which would be to take your lot to the zoning board of appeals.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.900
Don't necessarily

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:52.140
think you go that way. I think you do the best you can

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:55.180
with putting your signs out there

00:17:55.535 --> 00:17:56.335
and

00:17:56.415 --> 00:17:57.695
agent Halsey

00:17:58.015 --> 00:17:59.935
is yet to go

00:18:03.695 --> 00:18:11.180
make a fuss with anybody without sitting down and talking to him about what his concern is first. And I'm sure that

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:12.780
would be his

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.660
practice in this case.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:23.820
But as you mentioned the woods thing, know, on my walk there's

00:18:23.335 --> 00:18:29.415
a sign out there right now. Don't know who it came from, but it's in a heavily wooded area on Lake Road

00:18:29.975 --> 00:18:31.655
and it talks about,

00:18:33.575 --> 00:18:35.255
let's put a clouse on your house.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:39.860
You know, don't know who put it there. Been awful tempted to

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:45.780
just go yank it up. It's been there for a long time, but I haven't wanted to do that. I'm

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.580
