00:26:42.885 --> 00:26:43.845
One of those,

00:26:44.085 --> 00:26:45.685
one of the items in there

00:26:46.405 --> 00:26:49.605
covered accessory dwelling units. If

00:26:49.765 --> 00:26:53.685
somebody, if there's anybody that doesn't know what that is, that's putting,

00:26:54.005 --> 00:26:56.005
you know, a little apartment

00:26:56.420 --> 00:27:00.260
attached to your house or in the upstairs of a

00:27:00.820 --> 00:27:03.140
garage or a barn or something like that.

00:27:04.900 --> 00:27:05.540
And

00:27:05.940 --> 00:27:06.820
Andover

00:27:06.980 --> 00:27:07.780
has

00:27:07.780 --> 00:27:09.220
regulations

00:27:09.345 --> 00:27:13.345
in our zoning regs now about how we go about doing that.

00:27:15.425 --> 00:27:20.865
But the public act put in a requirement that I didn't think was in the town's

00:27:21.105 --> 00:27:21.905
best interest.

00:27:24.700 --> 00:27:26.940
So the Public Act 2129

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:31.180
requires that each town designate locations or zoning districts

00:27:31.340 --> 00:27:34.700
within the municipality in which accessory apartments are allowed.

00:27:35.865 --> 00:27:44.825
Then it goes on, provided that at least one accessory apartment shall be allowed as of right on each lot that contains a single family dwelling.

00:27:45.705 --> 00:27:48.025
Then it goes on to say no accessory apartment

00:27:48.140 --> 00:27:51.660
shall be required to be an affordable accessory apartment.

00:27:56.860 --> 00:27:57.500
So

00:27:58.060 --> 00:27:59.580
in our Lake District,

00:27:59.580 --> 00:28:04.365
you know, we've got a lot of very small building lots,

00:28:05.725 --> 00:28:07.165
as you're probably aware of,

00:28:08.285 --> 00:28:13.725
some of which, you know, downwards, you know, a fifth of an acre or something like that.

00:28:14.500 --> 00:28:16.980
And and so to

00:28:16.980 --> 00:28:20.900
put essentially a second house on that wouldn't be. Peskin:

00:28:22.580 --> 00:28:25.860
conducive to maintaining the water quality of the lake

00:28:26.515 --> 00:28:28.115
Our current regulations

00:28:28.675 --> 00:28:34.355
specify that we can put an accessory dwelling unit in the Lake District if

00:28:34.995 --> 00:28:36.835
the lot is greater than three acres.

00:28:39.120 --> 00:28:45.920
Some you can argue that that might be a little excessive that's the number that the Commission came up with to to

00:28:45.920 --> 00:28:48.160
maintain the water quality in the lake

00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:50.320
is as best we could.

00:28:51.200 --> 00:28:51.440
So.

00:28:56.815 --> 00:28:58.655
The process to opt out

00:28:59.135 --> 00:29:03.375
is that the Planning and Zoning Commission by two thirds vote

00:29:03.695 --> 00:29:07.615
votes to initiate the opt out process. We did that in our last meeting.

00:29:08.770 --> 00:29:11.730
Public hearing is held. That's what we're doing tonight.

00:29:13.250 --> 00:29:15.570
Once we've gotten input from the public,

00:29:15.810 --> 00:29:21.090
you know, the Commission can decide whether or not to opt out within the ordinary statutory deadlines,

00:29:21.090 --> 00:29:23.730
which is sixty five days after we close the hearing.

00:29:24.505 --> 00:29:28.505
We must state on the record what the reason is for making that decision.

00:29:29.145 --> 00:29:39.385
And, you know, primarily that reason is to maintain the water quality of Andover Lake by preventing accessory dwelling units on the very small lots in Lake District.

00:29:40.820 --> 00:29:44.020
We've got to publish our notice of decision, which is something

00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:45.380
we routinely do.

00:29:45.780 --> 00:29:49.860
And then it goes to the Board of Selectmen that by a two thirds vote,

00:29:53.355 --> 00:29:54.075
to

00:29:54.155 --> 00:29:55.035
approve

00:29:55.195 --> 00:29:57.435
our results of the opt out process

00:29:57.755 --> 00:29:59.755
once we take it to them.

00:30:00.955 --> 00:30:01.435
If

00:30:03.675 --> 00:30:06.955
we have not done this by 01/01/2023,

00:30:07.480 --> 00:30:10.200
the requirements of the Public Act 2,129

00:30:10.200 --> 00:30:12.680
go into effect regardless of our regulations

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.560
and all those things that are in

00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:16.1000
the Public Act

00:30:17.400 --> 00:30:19.800
