you know, we stuck with the Lake District, which is consistent with our current regulations,

00:36:45.070 --> 00:36:47.550
is our rationale for opting out.

00:36:48.350 --> 00:36:49.310
Okay,

00:36:49.310 --> 00:36:49.870
thanks Jed.

00:36:52.165 --> 00:36:52.965
>> Any other

00:36:53.525 --> 00:36:56.245
questions from the public before we start?

00:36:59.845 --> 00:37:00.485
Okay.

00:37:02.165 --> 00:37:05.685
Hearing none, we'll move on to new business item 5A,

00:37:07.190 --> 00:37:07.990
application

00:37:07.990 --> 00:37:09.830
20 two-two,

00:37:09.830 --> 00:37:12.710
proposed text amendment to section 15 of the

00:37:13.910 --> 00:37:15.590
handover zoning regulations.

00:37:18.675 --> 00:37:20.675
I make a motion that the.

00:37:22.995 --> 00:37:25.715
Section 15 to the draft

00:37:25.715 --> 00:37:30.435
of section 15 to the Andover zoning regulations on signs

00:37:30.595 --> 00:37:31.635
be approved.

00:37:32.275 --> 00:37:34.550
Second. Thank you, Steve.

00:37:36.150 --> 00:37:38.230
Any discussion from the Commission members?

00:37:45.995 --> 00:37:49.675
Hearing none, I will call for a roll call vote.

00:37:50.315 --> 00:37:51.035
Anne?

00:37:51.755 --> 00:37:52.555
Aye.

00:37:53.275 --> 00:37:54.875
>> Steve? Aye.

00:37:55.515 --> 00:37:56.955
Scott? Aye.

00:37:57.355 --> 00:37:57.915
Leanne?

00:37:58.840 --> 00:37:59.720
Aye.

00:37:59.960 --> 00:38:04.600
And I vote aye as well. The motion passes 500.

00:38:07.640 --> 00:38:09.000
Item 5B,

00:38:09.480 --> 00:38:10.280
application

00:38:10.280 --> 00:38:12.120
20 two-two

00:38:12.120 --> 00:38:14.945
proposed text amendment to section 17

00:38:15.265 --> 00:38:17.825
alcohol and cannabis establishments.

00:38:18.225 --> 00:38:20.545
I make a motion that section 17

00:38:21.025 --> 00:38:23.425
of the zoning regs draft

00:38:23.425 --> 00:38:25.665
for alcohol and cannabis establishments

00:38:25.665 --> 00:38:26.385
be approved.

00:38:28.220 --> 00:38:28.940
Second.

00:38:29.740 --> 00:38:31.100
>> Thank you, Leanne.

00:38:31.500 --> 00:38:32.700
Any discussion?

00:38:37.020 --> 00:38:38.220
Hearing none,

00:38:39.420 --> 00:38:41.020
do a roll call vote.

00:38:41.180 --> 00:38:41.580
Anne?

00:38:42.695 --> 00:38:43.655
Aye.

00:38:44.135 --> 00:38:44.935
Steve?

00:38:45.015 --> 00:38:45.895
Aye.

00:38:46.215 --> 00:38:47.655
Scott? Aye.

00:38:48.055 --> 00:38:48.935
Leanne?

00:38:49.495 --> 00:38:50.375
Aye.

00:38:50.855 --> 00:38:52.935
>> And I vote aye as well.

00:38:57.670 --> 00:38:59.270
New business 5C.

00:39:00.470 --> 00:39:05.350
8Dash8Dash24

00:39:05.350 --> 00:39:11.350
referral referral repurpose the old firehouse located at 15 Center Street for usage parking

00:39:11.565 --> 00:39:13.645
for the town's senior transportation

00:39:13.645 --> 00:39:14.605
vehicles

00:39:14.605 --> 00:39:16.525
and auxiliary storage.

00:39:18.605 --> 00:39:19.645
At this point,

00:39:20.205 --> 00:39:24.045
I will turn the discussion over to you, Eric. I saw

00:39:24.390 --> 00:39:25.110
an

00:39:25.270 --> 00:39:32.390
update to the 08/24 letter that I thought had some great information in it. And if you could share that with the Commission, I'd appreciate it.

00:39:34.790 --> 00:39:36.790
Certainly. Can I share my screen here?

00:39:37.935 --> 00:39:42.815
>> Yes, you can. And Scott, if you could mute yourself so we won't get that feedback, that'd be great. Thank you.

00:39:52.670 --> 00:39:53.390
>> Hopefully

00:39:53.790 --> 00:39:56.670
you're looking at a picture of a memorandum

00:39:56.670 --> 00:39:57.630
from me.

00:39:58.030 --> 00:40:01.950
I'm not going to read the whole thing but I'll just go over the highlights

00:40:02.750 --> 00:40:03.630
of it.

00:40:04.670 --> 00:40:06.815
What this is, is a

00:40:09.295 --> 00:40:10.815
statutory referral

00:40:10.815 --> 00:40:13.295
on behalf of the Board of Selectmen

00:40:13.295 --> 00:40:15.215
for municipal improvement

00:40:15.535 --> 00:40:17.215
at 15 Center Street.

00:40:17.880 --> 00:40:24.440
So, the town already owns the land at a property and existing structure at 15 Center Street.

00:40:25.240 --> 00:40:30.920
That existing structure originally dated back to the earliest parts of it were from around 1860.

00:40:31.305 --> 00:40:34.425
It's been expanded multiple times since then.

00:40:34.665 --> 00:40:37.785
The town has owned it since 1938

00:40:37.785 --> 00:40:38.265
and

00:40:38.985 --> 00:40:41.545
we used it as a fire station

00:40:41.545 --> 00:40:47.400
for like fifty two or fifty three years before it was abandoned in use for that.

00:40:47.960 --> 00:40:51.320
We continued to use it as a senior center

00:40:51.320 --> 00:40:53.480
after the 1990s.

00:40:54.760 --> 00:40:57.640
It currently has the ability to park.

00:40:58.200 --> 00:41:00.965
It has four bays in it currently.

00:41:02.565 --> 00:41:03.205
So,

00:41:03.525 --> 00:41:05.445
in 2018,

00:41:05.925 --> 00:41:12.325
the town did a survey of the property because a number of people have been complaining about mold in the building.

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:15.320
And based on some environmental

00:41:15.320 --> 00:41:16.120
studies

00:41:16.200 --> 00:41:18.920
determined to stop using it for

00:41:19.800 --> 00:41:20.520
a

00:41:20.680 --> 00:41:25.705
senior center because of the excessively high mold counts and problems with it.

00:41:26.425 --> 00:41:28.505
They looked into both remediation

00:41:29.065 --> 00:41:34.985
and eventually determined that it was not worth due to the age of the structure and inherent problems,

00:41:35.145 --> 00:41:36.585
it was not worth

00:41:37.625 --> 00:41:38.825
trying to fix it up.

00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:44.020
At this point, the structure is deteriorated to the point that

00:41:44.980 --> 00:41:50.260
we're concerned about the roof on the Far Bay actually caving in with vehicles in there.

00:41:52.275 --> 00:41:56.595
We're looking to address this sometime sooner rather than later.

00:41:57.315 --> 00:42:00.435
The board of selectmen has authorized me to

00:42:00.995 --> 00:42:02.915
apply for a steep grant

00:42:02.995 --> 00:42:04.435
to demolish

00:42:04.435 --> 00:42:05.555
this building

00:42:05.690 --> 00:42:11.290
and build the new four bay vehicle storage facility at the same location.

00:42:12.090 --> 00:42:15.210
Because this would clearly be a significant improvement,

00:42:15.930 --> 00:42:16.490
the

00:42:17.050 --> 00:42:18.570
Planning and Zoning Commission

00:42:19.925 --> 00:42:24.325
has to ensure that it is consistent with the plan of conservation and development.

00:42:25.925 --> 00:42:26.565
So,

00:42:28.245 --> 00:42:33.525
there's some other stuff that's going to need to happen. It's going to need to go before ZBA for some variances,

00:42:34.210 --> 00:42:36.290
both the use variants and then

00:42:38.290 --> 00:42:40.210
variants for the side

00:42:40.370 --> 00:42:42.690
and front yard setbacks.

00:42:44.050 --> 00:42:48.465
But what we're going to build in its place is a smaller structure than what's there now

00:42:49.105 --> 00:42:51.745
that will decrease the nonconformity

00:42:51.745 --> 00:42:56.385
of the building. It won't eliminate it, but it will decrease it from where it is currently.

00:42:56.865 --> 00:43:02.670
What we're talking about building is basically a 36x60 foot wide parking garage,

00:43:03.150 --> 00:43:05.230
but do it in such a way that it

00:43:05.630 --> 00:43:06.750
has some

00:43:07.870 --> 00:43:09.150
so that it looks

00:43:09.390 --> 00:43:15.905
appropriate for that neighborhood. We're not just going to build a, you know, a big metal shed to put all the vehicles

00:43:16.305 --> 00:43:16.945
in.

00:43:17.905 --> 00:43:18.385
Understand

00:43:18.785 --> 00:43:20.625
that this is a residential

00:43:20.705 --> 00:43:21.505
neighborhood.

00:43:22.385 --> 00:43:25.665
One of the reasons why we're looking at this location

00:43:26.220 --> 00:43:30.540
is because this location currently has three phase power available.

00:43:31.660 --> 00:43:34.540
And with the state's push towards electrification

00:43:34.540 --> 00:43:35.660
of vehicles,

00:43:35.900 --> 00:43:41.020
we're cognizant of the fact that we're probably going to need to at some point install

00:43:41.185 --> 00:43:43.185
DC fast chargers

00:43:43.265 --> 00:43:44.865
so we can charge,

00:43:45.585 --> 00:43:47.345
you know, senior transportation

00:43:47.345 --> 00:43:48.065
buses,

00:43:48.625 --> 00:43:57.690
electric buses, because I think that's coming, whether it comes next year or five years from now, the town's going to have to deal with that in some form or another.

00:43:58.330 --> 00:43:58.810
So,

00:43:59.370 --> 00:44:01.050
the question turns to

00:44:01.530 --> 00:44:03.130
what does the POCD

00:44:03.130 --> 00:44:05.450
say relative to this application?

00:44:06.490 --> 00:44:10.010
So, I went through the POCD and looked at the areas where

00:44:10.705 --> 00:44:11.585
this is

00:44:12.145 --> 00:44:13.425
in conformance.

00:44:13.505 --> 00:44:17.665
And then we'll talk a little bit about where it's not quite in conformance.

00:44:18.305 --> 00:44:20.305
First thing, the

00:44:20.305 --> 00:44:29.400
POCD is clear that the median age of residents is increasing dramatically and that there will be an increased need for senior transportation.

00:44:30.440 --> 00:44:38.245
That is really why the town is anticipating the need for a couple of buses and a couple of smaller vehicles

00:44:39.045 --> 00:44:40.165
going forward.

00:44:41.205 --> 00:44:47.925
The other thing to note is that the town of Andover has very little business in industrially zone land,

00:44:48.165 --> 00:44:50.485
less than 9% of the total land area.

00:44:51.390 --> 00:44:53.470
We're predominantly residential.

00:44:53.950 --> 00:44:54.510
So,

00:44:57.230 --> 00:45:01.390
the reality is any spot we're going to put senior transportation

00:45:01.390 --> 00:45:02.030
in

00:45:02.750 --> 00:45:05.230
is probably zoned residential

00:45:05.265 --> 00:45:07.825
because there's just not a lot of industrial,

00:45:08.145 --> 00:45:12.305
you know, or business zone property where we're likely going to be able to put this.

00:45:13.985 --> 00:45:15.105
So again,

00:45:15.345 --> 00:45:16.865
in chapter 12,

00:45:17.025 --> 00:45:20.225
the POCD talks about the case for the aging population

00:45:20.670 --> 00:45:23.150
and the need to be able to provide transportation

00:45:23.150 --> 00:45:27.150
services for them, which is exactly what this is

00:45:29.070 --> 00:45:30.190
pointing towards.

00:45:30.910 --> 00:45:32.350
In chapter 10,

00:45:32.990 --> 00:45:34.830
remember this POC

00:45:35.295 --> 00:45:36.415
was written

00:45:36.495 --> 00:45:40.655
when this building was in use as a senior center.

00:45:41.135 --> 00:45:44.495
So keep that in mind that go back seven years,

00:45:45.055 --> 00:45:46.975
this was a functioning building.

00:45:47.480 --> 00:45:56.920
And although we talked a lot about where we were going to potentially put a new senior center going forward, we still had a senior center available to the town.

00:45:57.720 --> 00:46:00.600
There is a mention in chapter 10

00:46:00.825 --> 00:46:04.025
about developing the Center Street area

00:46:04.265 --> 00:46:06.425
as part of the main

00:46:06.425 --> 00:46:07.305
central

00:46:08.265 --> 00:46:10.025
kind of hub of the town.

00:46:10.585 --> 00:46:16.185
And, you know, the indication that it would be a good area to allow both multifamily housing,

00:46:16.640 --> 00:46:18.960
as well as mixed use development.

00:46:20.320 --> 00:46:21.360
In this case,

00:46:21.760 --> 00:46:23.840
well, that's I think a good worthwhile

00:46:23.840 --> 00:46:24.560
goal.

00:46:25.120 --> 00:46:26.640
This is impractical

00:46:26.640 --> 00:46:28.800
on this particular lot

00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:31.200
due to septic constraints on the property.

00:46:32.085 --> 00:46:38.805
So, as many of you know, the town at one point tried to buy the property across the street, 12 Center Street,

00:46:39.125 --> 00:46:46.660
because that's what it would have taken at the time to have a big enough leach field for us to put in a reasonably sized

00:46:46.900 --> 00:46:47.940
community

00:46:47.940 --> 00:46:49.620
center with the kind of

00:46:50.500 --> 00:46:52.660
stuff that we as a town wanted.

00:46:53.300 --> 00:46:55.700
Without that, when we looked at it initially,

00:46:55.995 --> 00:46:57.115
we determined

00:46:57.115 --> 00:46:59.995
we couldn't put any reasonable building there.

00:47:00.475 --> 00:47:07.115
That's another way of saying you probably could tear that building down and put in a single family house,

00:47:07.355 --> 00:47:12.530
but you're probably not going to be able to tear it down and put in a multi family or a bigger structure

00:47:13.250 --> 00:47:14.050
in there.

00:47:15.170 --> 00:47:19.890
So, while the POCD would envision more intensive development for that property,

00:47:20.210 --> 00:47:22.290
I don't think that's really practical

00:47:22.770 --> 00:47:27.565
because the topography is in the way and you have a series of septic constraints.

00:47:29.325 --> 00:47:31.485
The other thing I would note is that

00:47:31.805 --> 00:47:33.085
among the uses

00:47:33.565 --> 00:47:38.845
that are appropriate in the area designated as town center, which is not

00:47:39.725 --> 00:47:40.365
just

00:47:40.845 --> 00:47:44.500
Center Street, Center Street plus 316

00:47:44.580 --> 00:47:46.740
plus the area of Long Hill.

00:47:48.340 --> 00:47:52.500
You know between there and the ball field is governmental uses

00:47:52.660 --> 00:47:57.380
and a parking structure for senior transportation would definitely qualify

00:47:57.105 --> 00:48:00.145
as a government, you know, a governmental use.

00:48:00.945 --> 00:48:06.945
And lastly, this plan would also allow for future construction of a playground on the upper area

00:48:08.065 --> 00:48:09.185
of that property.

00:48:10.530 --> 00:48:11.890
So again,

00:48:13.570 --> 00:48:15.490
where this is contra

00:48:15.570 --> 00:48:16.450
indicated

00:48:16.930 --> 00:48:20.850
is chapter 10 item number seven of the POCD,

00:48:21.090 --> 00:48:24.210
which seeks to encourage housing in and near the town center.

00:48:24.645 --> 00:48:26.725
And this definitely would not

00:48:27.605 --> 00:48:28.405
encourage

00:48:28.405 --> 00:48:30.405
housing near the town center,

00:48:31.125 --> 00:48:34.245
but it would take just a single buildable

00:48:34.645 --> 00:48:36.820
bot for a single family house out

00:48:37.300 --> 00:48:42.100
of that. So while it would be possible to create infill housing

00:48:42.180 --> 00:48:43.940
at 15 Center Street,

00:48:44.260 --> 00:48:45.460
I think that

00:48:45.700 --> 00:48:47.060
it's more valuable

00:48:47.540 --> 00:48:49.700
to the town to provide,

00:48:49.940 --> 00:48:53.635
you know, a centrally located senior transportation hub.

00:48:54.755 --> 00:48:59.395
So, that's kind of the argument we're making regarding the POCD.

00:49:00.035 --> 00:49:01.715
And this is a picture

00:49:01.955 --> 00:49:02.675
of

00:49:03.475 --> 00:49:05.730
what it looks like now.

00:49:06.930 --> 00:49:10.370
Most of you know driven by there, it's a pretty dilapidated

00:49:10.370 --> 00:49:11.250
structure.

00:49:12.130 --> 00:49:13.650
The front facade

00:49:14.050 --> 00:49:14.850
is

00:49:14.850 --> 00:49:17.410
in rough shape. The whole thing's kind of in rough shape.

00:49:18.095 --> 00:49:25.695
So, that's what we have now and I'm going to share real quick a picture of what the town is anticipating

00:49:25.775 --> 00:49:26.495
putting there.

00:49:33.390 --> 00:49:35.550
And so that is the facade.

00:49:35.630 --> 00:49:38.350
You can kind of get a feeling for scale.

00:49:40.030 --> 00:49:42.910
And this will be built into the hillside.

00:49:43.465 --> 00:49:47.145
So although it looks like a pretty tall building,

00:49:47.465 --> 00:49:52.345
remember due to the slopes, the backside of this building will only be exposed.

00:49:53.065 --> 00:49:54.265
The roofline

00:49:54.265 --> 00:49:57.305
will only start about two feet or three feet above

00:49:57.800 --> 00:49:58.680
the earth.

00:50:00.040 --> 00:50:04.200
The front facade will be exposed, but it will be set into the hillside

00:50:04.200 --> 00:50:06.200
in roughly the same position

00:50:07.160 --> 00:50:08.200
it is now.

00:50:09.000 --> 00:50:11.960
That is basically all I have unless

00:50:12.375 --> 00:50:19.015
you all have questions for me. Do you want me to leave this image up or do you want to go back to being able to see people?

00:50:19.735 --> 00:50:23.655
>> Let's go back to seeing everybody here. Thank you. Okay.

00:50:26.390 --> 00:50:30.710
Any Commission members have any questions or comments concerning

00:50:31.430 --> 00:50:33.990
the presentation that Eric just put on for us?

00:50:38.515 --> 00:50:43.635
>> I like the idea and especially that you could possibly put a playground

00:50:43.635 --> 00:50:45.875
in on the upper level in the future

00:50:46.035 --> 00:50:47.875
that would be good we need that.

00:50:50.275 --> 00:50:50.755
Okay

00:50:53.560 --> 00:50:54.600
Anybody else?

00:50:55.640 --> 00:50:59.320
>> Yeah, Eric, you mentioned that there were limited other

00:50:59.880 --> 00:51:01.160
town properties

00:51:01.560 --> 00:51:02.840
that could

00:51:03.880 --> 00:51:05.640
house a facility of this type.

00:51:06.205 --> 00:51:13.165
Did the town explore that and are there any other options or is this pretty much the only place we think we could put it?

00:51:14.045 --> 00:51:16.125
>> The

00:51:16.525 --> 00:51:19.645
public works foreman and I took an extensive survey

00:51:20.420 --> 00:51:23.940
and walked and looked at all the town properties

00:51:26.660 --> 00:51:28.500
that are potentials.

00:51:29.940 --> 00:51:30.740
The

00:51:30.980 --> 00:51:32.020
conclusion

00:51:32.020 --> 00:51:33.345
we reached is,

00:51:33.585 --> 00:51:38.785
so our original goal had been to locate this at the public works facility,

00:51:39.745 --> 00:51:41.745
because we already had a disturbed,

00:51:41.985 --> 00:51:43.985
you know, kind of industrial site.

00:51:44.305 --> 00:51:49.340
And it was next to the buses and it seemed like that would be, you know, a smart plan.

00:51:50.060 --> 00:51:55.260
But when we really started looking at that site, looking at where the existing driveways were,

00:51:55.420 --> 00:51:58.700
where the five hundred year floodplain

00:51:58.700 --> 00:52:00.585
was for the building,

00:52:00.745 --> 00:52:02.905
because we're not going to build the thing in a floodplain.

00:52:03.785 --> 00:52:08.825
You know, and took into account the side yard setbacks in that zone.

00:52:09.145 --> 00:52:12.665
We really didn't have a good option. It would have been possible

00:52:13.020 --> 00:52:14.700
to put it in that facility,

00:52:15.020 --> 00:52:16.620
but it would also have been,

00:52:17.100 --> 00:52:19.260
we would have had to shoehorn it in

00:52:19.980 --> 00:52:22.460
between there and the next neighbor.

00:52:22.540 --> 00:52:24.300
That would have required variances

00:52:24.300 --> 00:52:24.940
also,

00:52:25.100 --> 00:52:32.165
and it would have caused us problems plowing and getting access into the back of the area behind public works.

00:52:32.565 --> 00:52:34.245
We kind of looked

00:52:35.605 --> 00:52:36.805
at that and said,

00:52:37.125 --> 00:52:37.685
realistically,

00:52:37.925 --> 00:52:39.125
it would be doable,

00:52:39.205 --> 00:52:40.965
but it's not a good site.

00:52:41.900 --> 00:52:44.860
It's kind of a poor fit for what we were trying to do.

00:52:45.820 --> 00:52:47.900
We also looked at the area

00:52:48.140 --> 00:52:52.380
around the nature pond, the Doris Chamberlain nature pond.

00:52:52.780 --> 00:52:56.460
And again, there's physically enough room to locate the structure there,

00:52:57.135 --> 00:53:05.455
but it would eliminate the parking at the nature pond, which is desirable. And it would also have some pretty serious negative impacts potentially

00:53:05.615 --> 00:53:07.615
on that wetland ecosystem

00:53:07.615 --> 00:53:08.175
there.

00:53:08.815 --> 00:53:12.495
And we also looked at the area in and around the town hall

00:53:13.230 --> 00:53:14.670
because as you know,

00:53:15.150 --> 00:53:20.830
behind the town hall building, the town owns roughly 70 acres of land

00:53:21.630 --> 00:53:30.625
